{%- comment -%}
  ADAPTER: Courier / delivery-estimate provider swap point.

  Current state (native, no app): snippets/delivery-estimate.liquid
  validates the PIN is a real 6-digit format and shows the merchant's
  single configured default estimate (Theme settings -> Cart & shipping
  -> Default delivery estimate). It never fabricates a per-pincode ETA.

  To add real per-pincode/zone estimates from a courier API:
    1. Replace the click handler in sections/main-product.liquid's
       initDeliveryEstimate() with a fetch to the courier's rate/ETA
       endpoint (likely via an app proxy, since calling a third-party
       API with credentials directly from the storefront isn't safe).
    2. Keep the 6-digit format validation as a first-line client check.
    3. On any API failure/timeout, fall back to the existing default
       estimate text rather than showing an error - delivery info
       failing to load must never block browsing or Add to Cart.
{%- endcomment -%}
